S)"},{"label":"C","text":"Fusion Inhibitors"},{"label":"D","text":"Protease Inhibitors"},{"label":"E","text":"Integrase Inhibitors"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-21cad0446059","stem":"A 35 year old HIV positive male patient comes to the OPD with complaint of anorexia, nausea and vomiting and abdominal pain. His abdomen is tender in the epigastric area. Laboratory results reveal a raised serum amylase activity and a preliminary diagnosis is made of acute pancreatitis. Which of the following anti-retroviral drugs has the patient most likely been taking?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Saquinavir"},{"label":"B","text":"Zidovudine"},{"label":"C","text":"Didanosine"},{"label":"D","text":"Efavirenz"},{"label":"E","text":"Enfuvirtide"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ae0ef87ad98c","stem":"A 40 year old HIV positive patient is receiving HAART regimen (Highly active anti-retroviral therapy). Four weeks after initiating therapy, he comes to the emergency department complaining of severe pain in the flank, nausea and frequent urination. Which one of the following drugs is most likely the cause of his symptoms?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Zidovudine"},{"label":"B","text":"Indinavir"},{"label":"C","text":"Efavirenz"},{"label":"D","text":"Nevirapine"},{"label":"E","text":"Nelfinavir"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7e563643ca30","stem":"A 30 year old man is recently diagnosed with HIV and therapy is started. After the first week of therapy, the patient complains of headaches, irritability, and nightmares. Which one of the following anti-retroviral drugs is most likely to be causing these symptoms?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Efavirenz"},{"label":"B","text":"Indinavir"},{"label":"C","text":"Lamivudine"},{"label":"D","text":"Nevirapine"},{"label":"E","text":"Stavudine"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-71b7240efbd2","stem":"A 35 year old woman is diagnosed with chronic hepatitis B infection and therapy is initiated. Just after a few hours she comes to the emergency department complaining of fever, chills and muscle aches. Which one of the following drugs most likely caused these symptoms?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lamivudine"},{"label":"B","text":"Adefovir"},{"label":"C","text":"Entecavir"},{"label":"D","text":"Interferon alfa"},{"label":"E","text":"Ribavirin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-302611fa5193","stem":"A 60 year old man with known history of Parkinson’s disease is to receive prophylaxis against Influenza A virus. He is given a drug that is useful against Parkinson’s disease as well for prophylaxis against influenza. The drug with which of the following mechanisms of action is most likely to have been given?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It prevents entry and penetration of the virus"},{"label":"B","text":"It prevents uncoating of the virus"},{"label":"C","text":"It prevents replication of the virus"},{"label":"D","text":"It prevents assembly of newly synthesized virus particles"},{"label":"E","text":"It prevents release of the newly synthesized virus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b73364661b9f2d164df81bd1ead795f86c0f6fd9"},{"id":"q-d04982c5b7f7","stem":"Which of the following is the most important side effect of zidovudine?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antiviral","suggest