essing and virus assembly. 8. Group B","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pilocarpine"},{"label":"B","text":"Norepinephrine"},{"label":"C","text":"Lopinavir/Ritonavir"},{"label":"D","text":"Epinephrine"},{"label":"E","text":"Nevirapine"},{"label":"F","text":"Tetracycline"},{"label":"G","text":"Zidovudine"},{"label":"H","text":"ipratropium"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-00acbda09db9","stem":"All typical antipsychotic drugs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","topicOriginal":"Central Nervous System Drugs","subtopic":"Antipsychotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Have similar efficacies T"},{"label":"B","text":"Cause extrapyramidal side effects F"},{"label":"C","text":"Control negative symptoms better than positive symptoms F"},{"label":"D","text":"Have extrapyramidal side effects such as Parkinsonian symptoms T"},{"label":"E","text":"Have the disadvantage of not being available in an injectable form for noncompliant patients F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bf467bf2a10d","stem":"Typical antipsychotic drugs have the following properties","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","topicOriginal":"Central Nervous System Drugs","subtopic":"Antipsychotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Large volume of distribution T"},{"label":"B","text":"Longer duration of action than expected based on their half-lives T"},{"label":"C","text":"Potentiate sedation of benzodiazepines and antihistamines T"},{"label":"D","text":"Include clozapine F"},{"label":"E","text":"Include haloperidol T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9781acf2a29d","stem":"Bipolar disorder","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Includes mania, which can be precipitated by any antidepressant F"},{"label":"B","text":"First line therapy is valproate F"},{"label":"C","text":"First line therpy is carbamazepine F"},{"label":"D","text":"Drugs for bipolar disorder should never be given with antipsychotics or benzodiazepines F"},{"label":"E","text":"For one of the drugs for bipolar disorder, the blood level of the drug should be monitored T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-16fc11d4aaa7","stem":"Sedative-hypnotics","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Barbiturates are effective for treating anxiety T"},{"label":"B","text":"Buspirone is effective for treating anxiety T"},{"label":"C","text":"Zolpidem is effective for treating anxiety"},{"label":"D","text":"Barbiturates are effective for inducing hypnosis T"},{"label":"E","text":"Propranolol is effective for inducing hypnosis"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"f3186da2838f8d9ec7191be4cb9b05afa61c5766"},{"id":"q-10e3b418b171","stem":"Sedative-hypnotics","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"As sedatives, barbiturates and benzodiazepines have the same efficacy T"},{"label":"B","text":"As hypnotics, barbiturates and benzodiazepines have the same efficacy T"},{"label":"C","text":"Barbiturates and benzodiazepines have the same side effect profiles F"},{"label":"D","text":"Ethanol toxicity is independent of the rate of rise of ethanol blood level"},{"label":"E","text":"Is the most common cause of chronic pancreatitis F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"f3186da2838f8d9ec7191be4cb9b05afa61c5766"},{"id":"q-e4191ea7b9f5","stem":"Quantitative measures of pharmacokinetic parameters","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Pharmacokinetic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bioavailability is maximum for intravenously administered drugs"},{"label":"B","text":"The volume of distribution is larger for drugs distributed to more organs"},{"label":"C","text":"The rate of elimination of a drug is a measure of drug clearance"},{"label":"D","text":"The half-life of a drug is affected by its volume of distribution"},{"label":"E","text":"Drug metabolism involves molecular changes that usually increase the ability of the drug to be excreted"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6f01beb58a90","stem":"A patient presents with prostate hyperplasia or cancer. Which of the following drugs are used for these indications?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"GnRH analogue with long half-life"},{"label":"B","text":"Aromatase inhibitor"},{"label":"C","text":"The androgen receptor antagonist cyroterone acetate"},{"label":"D","text":"The androgen receptor antagonist flutamide"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-558766062613","stem":"A woman presents with estrogen-dependent breast cancer. After surgery, which of the following SERMs (selective estrogen receptor modulators) would be appropriate to give to decrease the likelihood of further tumors developing?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Receptor","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tamoxifen"},{"label":"B","text":"Raloxifene"},{"label":"C","text":"Toremifene"},{"label":"D","text":"Clomiphene"},{"label":"E","text":"Tamoxifen and toremifene combination"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-04f36f451f2b","stem":"Thyroid drugs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"131I concentrates in the thyroid, but cannot destroy this gland"},{"label":"B","text":"Propylthiouracil is the thioamine preferred for pregnant patients and inhibits 5’-deiodinase"},{"label":"C","text":"Carbimazole is a prodrug of methimazole"},{"label":"D","text":"Levothyroxine is a safe and effective drug for hyperthyroidism"},{"label":"E","text":"Thiocyanate is a radiopaque material with limited use due to the risk of aplastic anemia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","short_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5458c243dfc1","stem":"A patient with hyperthyroidism is scheduled for thyroid gland surgery. In order to reduce the size and vascularity of the thyroid gland, making it technically easier to excise, which of the following drugs would be given before surgery?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Thiocyanate, perchlorate, or pertechnetate"},{"label":"B","text":"131I"},{"label":"C","text":"Stable inorganic iodide"},{"label":"D","text":"Propylthiouracil"},{"label":"E","text":"Methimazole"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5c63bad7e982","stem":"Drug resistance to chemotherapeutic drugs is becoming a serious medical problem. Drug resistance can be caused by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bacterial transfer of plasmids"},{"label":"B","text":"Chemoprophylaxis"},{"label":"C","text":"Use of antibiotics that are not indicated for the clinical situation"},{"label":"D","text":"Insensitivity to apoptosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Combination chemotherapy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-73c772f0c69c","stem":"Strategies for beneficial drug combinations (to reduce resistance, improve efficacy, and/or decrease toxicity) include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Combining drugs that act at the same step to increase the rate of cell kill"},{"label":"B","text":"Combining drugs with the same toxicity, using maximum tolerated doses, to increase the rate of cell kill"},{"label":"C","text":"It is unlikely that mutations will emerge at the same time against several different drugs with the same mechanism of action"},{"label":"D","text":"Combining synergistic drugs and lowering their doses to decrease side effects"},{"label":"E","text":"Combining hormones, immunotherapies and biotherapies"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-30b70d1f0f45","stem":"Overdose treatment","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Includes determining the toxin"},{"label":"B","text":"Never relies on homeostatic mechanisms to limit the injury"},{"label":"C","text":"Should be treated with steps that include stabilizing the patient"},{"label":"D","text":"Includes removal of exposure as optional, after the patient is stabilized"},{"label":"E","text":"Includes toxicokinetics only if the toxin is identified"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c14fa4877fed","stem":"Treatment of overdoses or poisoning may include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hemoperfusion for inorganic salts T"},{"label":"B","text":"Fresh frozen plasma for coumadin F"},{"label":"C","text":"Methylene blue for nitrites T"},{"label":"D","text":"Penicillamine for lead poisoning T"},{"label":"E","text":"Flumazenil for barbiturate overdose F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"394edd274b657981b373269200121d067ab0bbe2"},{"id":"q-64815d09374c","stem":"Drug interactions with anesthetics, which should be considered for their adverse or beneficial effects include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","topicOriginal":"Central Nervous System Drugs","subtopic":"Anesthetic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Corticosteroid therapy"},{"label":"B","text":"Antiepilepsy drugs"},{"label":"C","text":"Antihypertensive agents"},{"label":"D","text":"β-adrenoceptor blocking drugs"},{"label":"E","text":"Diuretics"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-506aa000e507","stem":"Synergistic drug interactions include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Penicillin and aminoglycoside T"},{"label":"B","text":"Amphotericin B and flucytosine T"},{"label":"C","text":"Histamine and epinephrine"},{"label":"D","text":"Flumaxenil and benzodiazepine"},{"label":"E","text":"Morphine and naloxone F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-83d126c7a269","stem":"The choice of analgesics and anesthetics during pregnancy and labor should consider drug effects on the mother and fetus or newborn as follows","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","topicOriginal":"Central Nervous System Drugs","subtopic":"Anesthetic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pethidine delays labor more than morphine"},{"label":"B","text":"General anesthesia is preferred rather than local anesthesia for Cesarean sections"},{"label":"C","text":"Ketamine is preferred for patients with eclampsia or pre-eclampsia"},{"label":"D","text":"Sulphonamides are preferred to avoid adverse effects in the newborn"},{"label":"E","text":"β-adrenoreceptor blockers are useful to treat fetal response to hypoxia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Central Nervous System Drugs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c4f55ae0afbf","stem":"Pharmacokinetic changes occur in pregnancy due to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"General Pharmacology","topicOriginal":"General Pharmacology","subtopic":"Pharmacokinetic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"An increase in the volume of distribution based on increased total body water"},{"label":"B","text":"An increase in the volume of distribution based on increased fat"},{"label":"C","text":"An increase in liver metabolism based on an increase in liver function"},{"label":"D","text":"An increase in liver metabolism based on an increase in hepatic blood flow"},{"label":"E","text":"A decrease in eliminated based on a decrease in renal blood flow STUDENT VERSION Postgraduate Students Clinical Pharmacology 2007-2008 FINAL EXAM"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"General Pharmacology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c55ed3b50eee","stem":"B2 –Antagonist(eg.Salbutamol,Terbutaline)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Relax bronchial smooth muscles T"},{"label":"B","text":"Inhibit release of mast cell &other inflammatory mediators T"},{"label":"C","text":"Reduce heart rate F"},{"label":"D","text":"Cause vasoconstriction F"},{"label":"E","text":"Decrease intracellular cAMP F 4;Pharmacodynamics ;"},{"label":"A","text":"The fraction occupancy of a receptor predicts the extent of the effect of a drug T"},{"label":"B","text":"The efficacy of a drug is its EC50 F"},{"label":"C","text":"The potency of the drug is its EC50 T"},{"label":"D","text":"The therapeutic index of a drug is ED50/TD50 F"},{"label":"E","text":"Drug tolerance causes a shift of the dose respond curve to the right T 5;Acute goute is treated with"},{"label":"A","text":"NSAIDS such as asprin F"},{"label":"B","text":"Glucocorticoids as first choice F"},{"label":"C","text":"Allupurinol F"},{"label":"D","text":"Colchicine T"},{"label":"E","text":"Sulfinpyrazone F"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"cf3a848160d9c740140c01f19a55942127c0c72c"},{"id":"q-2ee20951a9d5","stem":"B2 –Agonist (eg.Salbutamol,Terbutaline)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Relax bronchial smooth muscles T"},{"label":"B","text":"Inhibit release of mast cell &other inflammatory mediators T"},{"label":"C","text":"Reduce heart rate F"},{"label":"D","text":"Cause vasoconstriction F"},{"label":"E","text":"Decrease intracellular cAMP F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5cee5940192b","stem":"Acute gout is treated with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicO