Pharmacology","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Reduction of hepatic output of glucose. T"},{"label":"B","text":"Reduction of protein synthesis. F"},{"label":"C","text":"Enhanced transport of potassium into cells T."},{"label":"D","text":"Increased glucose uptake in peripheral tissues. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Down regulation of insulin receptors when its concentration is high: a factor in the insulin resistance of obese diabetics. T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Endocrine Pharmacology · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","short_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"da78919f35f45898cbd29370b85a5476d035d5c2"},{"id":"q-d45be19e72df","stem":"The following statement about therapy with iron is true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Parenteral administration produces a more rapid rise in haemoglobin than oral administration. T"},{"label":"B","text":"Desferrioxamine is useful in the treatment over dosage with iron preparation T"},{"label":"C","text":"Ascorbic acid impairs the efficiency of iron absorption F"},{"label":"D","text":"Iron preparation should not be taken at same time as with tea which contains tannate. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Gastro-intestinal contains side effects which limit the use of oral iron preparations. T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["