rol. T"},{"label":"B","text":"Is particulary useful in heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia. F"},{"label":"C","text":"Acts locally on HMGCoA reductase in the intestine. F"},{"label":"D","text":"Is associated with rhabdomyolysis. T"},{"label":"E","text":"Is ineffective if prescribed with bile acid binding resin. F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1a9687d5a84ad13df745942fc19f3a211cf7bed5"},{"id":"q-3462baf0bf29","stem":"HDL (High density lipoproteins)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has anti-atherogenic lipoprotein. T"},{"label":"B","text":"Retrieves cholesterol from artery wall. T"},{"label":"C","text":"Promotes oxidation of atherogenic lipoprotein. F"},{"label":"D","text":"In high levels is an independent risk factor for coronary disease. F"},{"label":"E","text":"Is metabolized to low density lipoprotein. F"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"7f0b6af355e3e040850ea257e3ccf097451ff339"},{"id":"q-21cedf739c2d","stem":"Asprin will antagonize the antihypertensive effect of bendrofluazide because asprin","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Cardiovascular Drugs","top