","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Binding to the 30S ribosomal subunit"},{"label":"B","text":"Binding to topoisomerase II"},{"label":"C","text":"Binding to peptidyl transferase"},{"label":"D","text":"Inhibition of the synthesis of mycolic acids"},{"label":"E","text":"Inhibition of peptidoglycan transpeptidation"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"c44d81dfbc5382cdfecf75f903eeff64f14f9274"},{"id":"q-883c14e6d95b","stem":"Which of the following microorganisms are sensitive to aminoglycoside antibiotics? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antibiotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Clostridium difficile"},{"label":"B","text":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa"},{"label":"C","text":"Bacteroides fragilis"},{"label":"D","text":"Borrelia recurrentis"},{"label":"E","text":"Neisseria gonorrhea"},{"label":"F","text":"Klebsiella pneumoniae"},{"label":"G","text":"Escherichia coli"},{"label":"H","text":"Mycoplasma pneumoniae I) Legionella pneumophila"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"f8810fbdd99114006f6f2ccc69d81670499f970a"},{"id":"q-19c511cfff61","stem":"Which of the following statements regarding the toxicity of aminoglycosides are correct? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Allergic reactions are very common and often serious"},{"label":"B","text":"The risk of toxicity of these drugs is increased in patients with auditory impairment"},{"label":"C","text":"The risk of ototoxicity is increased in patients with renal failure"},{"label":"D","text":"Ototoxicity is irreversible"},{"label":"E","text":"Nephrotoxicity is reversible"},{"label":"E","text":"Nephrotoxicity is reversible if the drug is discontinued, but can otherwise lead to renal insufficiency"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"edbcf22cb3920bf50463366df330bd2df4bf90b5"},{"id":"q-8ec40972131f","stem":"A 33-year-old woman with type I diabetes is admitted to the hospital with fever (102F), shaking chills, nausea and vomiting, flank pain and hematuria. She has been suffering from chronic lower urinary tract infection for one year. The predominant pathogen of the infection was found to be Pseudomonas aeruginosa. The most appropriate treatment for this patient would include which of the following pairs of drugs?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Piperacillin and tobramycin"},{"label":"B","text":"Ampicillin and gentamicin"},{"label":"C","text":"Imipenem and erythromycin"},{"label":"D","text":"Cephalothin and amikacin"},{"label":"E","text":"Ampicillin and doxycycline"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1be8d8c85acbb2c38193c3c2272f088a335939bb"},{"id":"q-1e1262ce70ba","stem":"A 30-year-old male heroin addict, who had his tricuspid valve replaced 8 months ago, was readmitted to the hospital with a two days history of fever, shaking chills, rigors and night sweats. His vital sings were: BP 100/60 mm Hg, pulse 120 bpm, respirations 24/min, temperature 103.7 F. Two-dimensional echocardiography revealed three small vegetations on the prosthetic valve. Empiric therapy with amphotericin B, vancomycin and gentamicin was initiated. Three blood cultures were drawn and they were positive for Pseudomonas aeruginosa. A surgical excision of the infected valve and a 6 week postoperative treatment was planned. Which of the following pairs of drugs would be most appropriate for this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Amphotericin B and clindamycin"},{"label":"B","text":"Cefotaxime and tobramycin"},{"label":"C","text":"Metronidazole and gentamicin"},{"label":"D","text":"Vancomycin and erythromycin"},{"label":"E","text":"Piperacillin and cefazolin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-492a39a90ebe","stem":"Which of the following statements best explains the mechanism of action of macrolides?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inhibition of DNA-dependent RNA polymerase"},{"label":"B","text":"Blockade of the formation of ribosomal initiation complex"},{"label":"C","text":"Blockade of peptide bond formation"},{"label":"D","text":"Blockade of translocation"},{"label":"E","text":"Inhibition of transpeptidase enzymes"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2d45e37ee9e5","stem":"Which of the following is the primary cellular site of action of clarithromycin?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The cytoplasmic bacterial membranes"},{"label":"B","text":"The outer bacterial membrane"},{"label":"C","text":"The porin channels"},{"label":"D","text":"The peptidoglycan layer"},{"label":"E","text":"The microsomes"},{"label":"F","text":"The mitochondria"},{"label":"G","text":"The ribosomes"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"80b6b535ff8490f57153972d72c92a2c109a69bd"},{"id":"q-aa05679dbad4","stem":"Which of the following microorganisms are sensitive to macrolides? (check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pseudomonas aeruginosa"},{"label":"B","text":"Helicobacter pylori"},{"label":"C","text":"Shigella dysenteriae"},{"label":"D","text":"Klebsiella pneumoniae"},{"label":"E","text":"Bacteroides fragilis"},{"label":"F","text":"Bordetella pertussis"},{"label":"G","text":"Herpes simplex virus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-098d4dabb6c3","stem":"Which of the following microorganisms are sensitive to azithromycin? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mycoplasma pneumoniae"},{"label":"B","text":"Klebsiella pneumoniae"},{"label":"C","text":"Chlamydia pneumoniae"},{"label":"D","text":"Candida albicans"},{"label":"E","text":"Mycobacterium avium complex"},{"label":"F","text":"Giardia lamblia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-746824b15cbd","stem":"Bacterial resistance to macrolides may be due to which of the following mechanisms? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Active drug efflux from the bacterial cell"},{"label":"B","text":"Reduced uptake of the drug by the bacterial cell"},{"label":"C","text":"Altered ribosomal binding site which prevents drug binding"},{"label":"D","text":"Production of acetyl transferase enzymes that inactivate the drug"},{"label":"E","text":"Production of phosphoryl transferase enzymes that inactivate the drug"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-83f49492a3a0","stem":"Which of the following statements about the resistance to macrolide antibiotics are correct? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antibiotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is exceedingly rare"},{"label":"B","text":"It is completely crossed among different macrolides"},{"label":"C","text":"It is partially crossed between macrolides and aminoglycosides"},{"label":"D","text":"It is common for Bacteroides fragilis and Pseudomonas aeruginosa"},{"label":"E","text":"It is usually acquired by a plasmid-mediated transfer"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f9d00d20a94a","stem":"Which of the following drugs can be used to treat infections due to Mycobacterium avium complex in patients with AIDS?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Ampicillin"},{"label":"B","text":"Tetracycline"},{"label":"C","text":"Clarithromycin"},{"label":"D","text":"Metronidazole"},{"label":"E","text":"Vancomycin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1661b811efccd75de920777b41eff62f1df5445b"},{"id":"q-96632fbcf8f8","stem":"Which of the following statements correctly pairs the binding site of clindamycin with the action that follows that binding?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"30S ribosomal subunit - increased synthesis of lethal proteins"},{"label":"B","text":"Cytoplasmic membrane - depolarization"},{"label":"C","text":"30S ribosomal subunit - misreading of mRNA template"},{"label":"D","text":"50S ribosomal subunit - blockade of peptide bond formation"},{"label":"E","text":"Cell wall - blockade of cross-linking of the peptidoglycan chain"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"e8ee58bac535503a66f53b71b4eaf2e8b4f98946"},{"id":"q-bb2378735e1c","stem":"The primary clinical use of clindamycin is to treat which of the following infections?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Legionella"},{"label":"B","text":"Klebsiella"},{"label":"C","text":"Clostridium"},{"label":"D","text":"Mycobacterial"},{"label":"E","text":"Proteus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"fdaae3b1886ba864994569316157573836ca0dbb"},{"id":"q-ab7e2ca66d54","stem":"A 15-year-old girl complained of watery diarrhea. She was recently diagnosed with streptococcal pharyngitis and started treatment with erythromycin three days ago. Which of the following statements best explains the cause of the diarrhea in this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Erythromycin kills most bacteria of the intestinal flora"},{"label":"B","text":"Erythromycin inhibits water reabsorption by colonic mucosa"},{"label":"C","text":"Erythromycin stimulates motilin receptors in the gut"},{"label":"D","text":"It is caused by an allergic reaction to erythromycin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a73415d86313","stem":"A 22-year-old woman presented with fever and a very painful sore throat. The woman was otherwise healthy, but medical history was significant for a congenital long QT syndrome discovered six years ago. On physical examination the throat was erythematous with exudative patches. A Gram stain of the exudate showed many gram-positive bacteria. The patient was prescribed an antibiotic treatment. Which of the following drugs would be contraindicated in this woman?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antibiotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vancomycin"},{"label":"B","text":"Amoxicillin"},{"label":"C","text":"Cefepime"},{"label":"D","text":"Erythromycin"},{"label":"E","text":"Meropenem"},{"label":"F","text":"Rifampin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a88803a88ff4","stem":"A 15-day-old baby was admitted to pediatric ward with mucopurulent ocular discharge, edema of the eyelids and pseudomembrane formation. A Gram stain of the exudate revealed no microorganisms. A Giemsa's stain showed cytoplasmic inclusions consistent with an infection by Chlamydia trachomatis. Which of the following drugs would be most appropriate for this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tetracycline"},{"label":"B","text":"Erythromycin"},{"label":"C","text":"Metronidazole"},{"label":"D","text":"Vancomycin"},{"label":"E","text":"Ampicillin"},{"label":"F","text":"Tobramycin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bf9288745397","stem":"Which of the following statements about tetracyclines are correct? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are mainly bactericidal drugs for susceptible bacteria"},{"label":"B","text":"They are active against mycoplasma and chlamydia"},{"label":"C","text":"Most compounds do not cross the blood brain barrier even when meninges are inflamed"},{"label":"D","text":"They may cause the gray baby syndrome when given to the newborn"},{"label":"E","text":"They are chelating agents that bind to several cations including calcium"},{"label":"F","text":"They may accumulate in bone, dentine and teeth enamel"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"ebef7c6ece1709cdc18669e1f95628f5f7cc416e"},{"id":"q-b61d505e3a79","stem":"Which of the following microorganisms are sensitive to tetracyclines? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bacillus anthrancis"},{"label":"B","text":"Helicobacter pylori"},{"label":"C","text":"Bordetella pertussis"},{"label":"D","text":"Legionella pneumophila"},{"label":"E","text":"Clostridium difficile"},{"label":"F","text":"Borrelia burgdorferi"},{"label":"G","text":"Mycoplama pneumoniae"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0856c0555366","stem":"Bacterial resistance to tetracyclines may be due to which of the following mechanisms? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Production of an effusion pump that extrudes the drug from the bacterial cell"},{"label":"B","text":"Production of acetyl transferase enzymes that inactivate the drug"},{"label":"C","text":"Reduced permeability of the outer bacterial membrane to the drug"},{"label":"D","text":"Production of phosphoryl transferase enzymes that inactivate the drug"},{"label":"E","text":"Altered binding of the transpeptidase enzyme"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f4f32a6469f7","stem":"Which of the following are most likely adverse effects of tetracyclines? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Impairment of liver function"},{"label":"B","text":"Gray baby syndrome"},{"label":"C","text":"Seizures"},{"label":"D","text":"Dystonic reactions"},{"label":"E","text":"Tooth discoloration in young children"},{"label":"F","text":"Kernicterus in the newborn infants"},{"label":"G","text":"Photosensitivity"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"0a71a736efc7ae93704e251460ef2996ebd816ec"},{"id":"q-ee0c2f1418cc","stem":"Which of the following diseases is most likely caused by an idiosyncratic reaction to chloramphenicol?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Acute renal failure"},{"label":"B","text":"Acute liver necrosis"},{"label":"C","text":"Optic neuritis"},{"label":"D","text":"Gray baby syndrome"},{"label":"E","text":"Aplastic anemia"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-735543514edb","stem":"Which of the following antibiotics binds to the 50S ribosomal subunit and inhibits the formation of the initiation complex?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials","topicOriginal":"Antimicrobials","subtopic":"Antibiotic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Tetracycline"},{"label":"B","text":"Erythromycin"},{"label":"C","text":"Chloramphenicol"},{"label":"D","text":"Gentamicin"},{"label":"E","text":"Linezolid"},{"label":"F","text":"Rifampin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"50897b94152432ac58441d1c7bc0b3642b78166b"},{"id":"q-278b8e0bc788","stem":"Which of the following microorganisms are most sensitive to both macrolides and tetracyclines? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antimicrobials","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bacillus anthrancis"},{"label":"B","text":"Mycoplasma pneumoniae"},{"label":"C","text":"Chlamydia pneumoniae"},{"label":"D","text":"Helicobacter pylori"},{"label":"E","text":"Borrelia burgdorferi"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Antimicrobials · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7dcb71ac95d5","stem":"A 33-year-old woman presents with fatigue, low grade fever, muscle and joint pain, and multiple red rashes with a clear center. She stated that 20 days ago she was bitten on a arm by a tiny tick and that a circular skin lesion started at the bite site, expanded to 15 cm or so, and was followed by multiple, painless rashes. Which of the following drugs would be most appropriate for this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gentamicin"},{"label":"B","text":"Ciprofloxacin"},{"label":"C","text":"Trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole"},{"label":"D","text":"Doxycycline"},{"label":"E","text":"Vancomycin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a6cd6a414902","stem":"A 36-year-old man is admitted to the hospital with high fever, chills, tachycardia, vomiting and muscle pain. He had the same symptoms 10 days ago, just after a staying in a campground near the border with Mexico. The fever was high for 3 days, then cleared abruptly. A thick blood smear with Giemsa stain revealed many threadlike bacteria with large, irregular coils. Which of the following drugs would be most appropriate for this patient?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Streptomycin"},{"label":"B","text":"Vancomycin"},{"label":"C","text":"Doxycycline"},{"label":"D","text":"Daptomycin"},{"label":"E","text":"Fluconazole Nucleic Acid Syn Inhibitors"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0943b34c0d28","stem":"Which of the following statements regarding sulfonamides are correct? (Check all that apply)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They usually abruptly kill susceptible bacteria"},{"label":"B","text":"They are effective against Toxoplasma gondii"},{"label":"C","text":"They compete with para-aminobenzoic acid for the enzyme peptidyl transferase"},{"label":"D","text":"They are often given together with a dihydrofolate reductase inhibitor"},{"label":"E","text":"Most of them cannot cross the blood brain barrier even when meninges are inflamed"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e799f56c96a4","stem":"A 34-year-old woman with AIDS presents to the emergency room reporting 2 seizures in the past 24 hours. Physical signs include fever, altered mental status and a visual field defect. A magnetic resonance imaging of the head reveals several ring-shaped lesions in the brainstem. A brain biopsy shows crescent-shaped trophozoites within macrophages. Which of the following drug combinations would be appropriate to cure the patient's infection?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gentamicin and piperacillin"},{"label":"B","text":"Sulfadiazine and pyrimethamine"},{"label":"C","text":"Vancomycin and ceftazidime"},{"label":"D","text":"Isoniazid and rifampin"},{"label":"E","text":"Streptomycin 